365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 776 0 R
/ActualText (Build Size and Speed: CRA tends to have larger bundle sizes by default, as it includes many dependencies and configurations designed to work out of the box for a wide range of projects, while Vite, being more modern, produces smaller and faster builds by optimizing the dependencies it uses, reducing bundle sizes, and using advanced techniques like ES module imports.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 777 0 R
/ActualText (Configuration Flexibility: CRA provides a zero-config approach, which is great for beginners who want to start coding immediately, but it can be limited if you need to customize the build configuration, while Vite is highly configurable and allows developers to easily adjust settings for advanced needs like custom plugins or specific build optimizations.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
